OL,3,GNEWSAHow are sports clubs coping with
OL,4,Adrought?
OL,5,
OL,6,FCurrent drought conditions are
OL,7,Fthreatening to cause problems ahead of
OL,8,Fthe new sporting season, say many
OL,9,Fgrassroots clubs across the South East.
OL,11,FTeams have been warned about heading
OL,12,Fout on to bone-dry, cracked and uneven
OL,13,Fpitches caused by the prolonged hot and
OL,14,Fdry weather.
OL,16,FIt has led the FA to issue new guidance
OL,17,Fand the Rugby Football Union (RFU) to
OL,18,Fsuspend fixtures until late September,
OL,19,Fwith sides advised to speak to their
OL,20,Fgroundskeeper or pitch provider about
OL,21,Fpostponing or relocating games if
OL,22,Frequired.
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
